<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <Itf Name="IReadOnlyDictionary" Id="{511d635b-9ee9-475d-b527-1b8927b91e7e}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Associates generic keys with values.</summary>
<description>
Try lookup/removal operations contain exceptions without rolling back partial effects.
Generic query arguments are borrowed by default.
Explicitly requested release in Try operations is attempted even after lookup failure; caller-side
owning aliases are not reset.
OBJECT keys are permitted when their descriptors refer to live Object instances.
A borrowed key (IsMemoryOwner = FALSE) is not owned or destroyed by the dictionary; its owner must
keep it alive for every operation that may access the stored key.
An owned key must not be deleted or transferred to another owner through a caller-side alias.
While a key is stored, do not change data used by the active comparison rules, its equality/hash
results, or equality-relevant comparer configuration.
Remove the entry before such a change, then insert it again.
Queries and callbacks must not mutate keys or reenter collection mutation.
Do not use explicit query release to dispose of a stored key or other storage still retained by the
collection.
An address-based identity index must be rebuilt after address relocation; stale indices must not be
used.
Borrowing does not pin an object or extend its lifetime.
A copied object has its own identity; lookup using the original requires an equality strategy under
which original and copy are equal.
Default OBJECT lookup delegates to Object.Equals/GetHashCode; fields unrelated to equality/hash may
change.
Discard and populate the index again after equality-relevant address relocation before further
lookup.
Lookup uses one equality/hash strategy fixed for the collection lifetime; zero selects GENERIC_VALUE
default equality and hashing.
A custom comparer is borrowed, stays alive and retains stable equality-relevant configuration.
Empty descriptors are supported unless rejected by a validator.
No entry or enumeration order is guaranteed; a position is a current storage slot, not a sorted
rank.
Do not modify stored descriptors through returned references.
</description>
*)
(*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: © 2026 Oleksandr Tiutyk <trofimich@gmail.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
License: https://opensource.org/license/mit
*)

INTERFACE IReadOnlyDictionary EXTENDS ICollection]]></Declaration>
    <Method Name="ContainsGenericKey" Id="{9f8e7aad-b7e0-4834-94aa-20d7c5e1cdea}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Reports whether a matching entry exists for a borrowed generic query.</summary>
<description>
The query is borrowed by default.
Explicit release requests disposal of owned query storage after lookup completes, including a
missing result.
Requested release is attempted after both successful lookup and lookup failure. Before cleanup, the original framework exception is retained and a borrowed static system exception is cloned to preserve its code, catch point and timestamps across cleanup callbacks. The captured exception is then propagated through ExceptionManager.Throw in the current cyclic task; native errors use the framework SystemException representation. If capturing the system exception fails with terminal OOM, query cleanup is still attempted and terminal OOM takes precedence. Terminal allocation state is never cleared. Release is best effort and does not prove successful deallocation. Cleanup callbacks must not reenter collection mutation.
Release resets only the local descriptor copy; the caller must have disposal rights and must not
reuse or release owning aliases afterwards.
Borrowed payload is not freed.
</description>
*)
METHOD ContainsGenericKey : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	key : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
	releaseKey : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ContainsKey" Id="{ff9cfb18-10ca-467e-9680-e293c6b611d5}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Reports whether a matching raw query exists.</summary>
<description>
The raw ANY argument is borrowed without cloning or ownership transfer. keyIsObject = TRUE requires
a live Object function-block instance, not a pointer or interface variable.
FALSE uses ordinary runtime type mapping.
The caller keeps the query storage alive for the call.
</description>
*)
//!<param name="keyIsObject">Explicitly interprets the raw argument as a live Object instance.</param>
METHOD ContainsKey : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	key : ANY;
	keyIsObject : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="GetGenericKeyPosition" Id="{516cbd3d-5f27-4efd-8461-dc951eb682a7}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Returns the matching entry position, or a negative value when absent.</summary>
<description>
The query is borrowed by default.
Explicit release requests disposal of owned query storage after lookup completes, including a
missing result.
Requested release is attempted after both successful lookup and lookup failure. Before cleanup, the original framework exception is retained and a borrowed static system exception is cloned to preserve its code, catch point and timestamps across cleanup callbacks. The captured exception is then propagated through ExceptionManager.Throw in the current cyclic task; native errors use the framework SystemException representation. If capturing the system exception fails with terminal OOM, query cleanup is still attempted and terminal OOM takes precedence. Terminal allocation state is never cleared. Release is best effort and does not prove successful deallocation. Cleanup callbacks must not reenter collection mutation.
Release resets only the local descriptor copy; the caller must have disposal rights and must not
reuse or release owning aliases afterwards.
Borrowed payload is not freed.
The position is a current storage slot with no sorted-rank guarantee; mutation may invalidate it.
</description>
*)
METHOD GetGenericKeyPosition : DINT
VAR_INPUT
	key : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
	releaseKey : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="GetKeyPosition" Id="{5e2b0a29-a0f0-46ba-a9db-58fb22fe489f}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Returns the matching storage position, or a negative value when absent.</summary>
<description>
The raw ANY argument is borrowed without cloning or ownership transfer. keyIsObject = TRUE requires
a live Object function-block instance, not a pointer or interface variable.
FALSE uses ordinary runtime type mapping.
The caller keeps the query storage alive for the call.
The position is a current storage slot with no sorted-rank guarantee; mutation may invalidate it.
</description>
*)
//!<param name="keyIsObject">Explicitly interprets the raw argument as a live Object instance.</param>
METHOD GetKeyPosition : DINT
VAR_INPUT
	key : ANY;
	keyIsObject : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="GetKeyValuePairByIndex" Id="{621d17f0-ce5c-4e12-9107-2706dfc65ad4}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Borrows the entry at a current storage position.</summary>
<description>
The index must be within Length and is not a sorted rank; otherwise an exception is raised.
The returned descriptor reference and payload remain collection-owned or borrowed from their
original owner.
Do not mutate the descriptor or dispose of its payload through this view.
Mutation or destruction may invalidate the reference.
</description>
*)
METHOD GetKeyValuePairByIndex : REFERENCE TO TOF_Core.GENERIC_KEY_VALUE_PAIR
VAR_INPUT
	index : DINT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TryGetValueByGenericKey" Id="{2310dd19-0ba2-4860-a947-60f3473275c6}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Attempts to find a value by its key.</summary>
<description>
Returns TRUE when a value is found.
Use the output only on TRUE; no payload is cloned.
Catches exceptions without propagating them or clearing terminal allocation state.
Partial changes are not rolled back.
The query is borrowed by default.
When releaseKey is explicitly TRUE, attempts to release the supplied generic argument after
lookup/removal even on failure.
The caller must have disposal rights and must not reuse aliases of an owned argument after release.
A successful output is a borrowed descriptor copy; IsMemoryOwner does not transfer disposal rights
to the caller.
Stored payload must not be released through the output.
</description>
*)
METHOD TryGetValueByGenericKey : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	key : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
	releaseKey : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
	value : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TryGetValueByKey" Id="{c4542916-8eaf-41fb-a00c-f12b88d80700}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[(*!
<summary>Attempts to find a value by its key.</summary>
<description>
Returns TRUE when a value is found.
Use the output only on TRUE; no payload is cloned.
Catches exceptions without propagating them or clearing terminal allocation state.
Partial changes are not rolled back.
The raw ANY argument is borrowed without cloning or ownership transfer. keyIsObject = TRUE requires
a live Object function-block instance, not a pointer or interface variable.
FALSE uses ordinary runtime type mapping.
The caller keeps the query storage alive for the call.
A successful output is a borrowed descriptor copy; IsMemoryOwner does not transfer disposal rights
to the caller.
Stored payload must not be released through the output.
</description>
*)
//!<param name="keyIsObject">Explicitly interprets the raw argument as a live Object instance.</param>
METHOD TryGetValueByKey : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	key : ANY;
	keyIsObject : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
	value : TOF_Core.GENERIC_VALUE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    </Method>
  </Itf>
</TcPlcObject>